# Lesson 2, new hand: partner opens a strong two-bid, you raise. Student sits South.
title: Partner opens 2♥: raise with support
id: L02-27
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.5
student: S
board: 33
dealer: N
vulnerable: none

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  AK     AKQJ75 KQ4    82
  E  QT6    43     T987   KJ73
  S  9743   T86    J52    QT4
  W  J852   92     A63    A965

auction:
  N 2H     = 22+ points, five or more hearts: forcing
  E Pass
  S 3H*    = Heart support and a few points
     key: Partner's 2♥ is forcing. With three hearts and a smattering of high cards, raise.
     not Pass: Partner's two-bid is forcing. Did you remember you must bid once?
     not 2NT: 2NT is usually right, but with three-card support and a few points, can you show the fit at once?
     not 4H: 3♥ already shows support. Leave room for partner to decide.
     not *: With three hearts, can you raise partner?
  W Pass
  N 4H     = Game
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Partner knows what you have and chose 4♥. Pass.
     not *: Partner knows what you have and chose 4♥. Pass.
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Partner's 2♥ showed 22 or more points and at least five hearts, and you
  had to bid. Three hearts and a queen and a jack were enough to raise.
  That told partner about the fit, and she bid game. North is declarer,
  because she bid hearts first, and so East will lead to the first trick.

play:
  1   E DT  S D2  W DA  N D4
  2   W S2  N SA  E S6  S S3
  3   N HA  E H3  S H6  W H2
      note: Declarer draws trumps.
  4   N HK  E H4  S H8  W H9
      note: Two rounds, and the trumps are gone.
  5   N SK  E ST  S S4  W S5
      note: Declarer cashes the other spade winner.
  6   N DK  E D7  S D5  W D3
      note: Now the diamond winners.
  7   N DQ  E D8  S DJ  W D6
      note: And the ♦Q.
  8   N HQ  E D9  S HT  W S8
      note: Declarer runs the hearts.
  9   N HJ  E C3  S S7  W C5
      note: More hearts.
  10  N H7  E C7  S S9  W C6
      note: More hearts.
  11  N H5  E SQ  S C4  W SJ
      note: The last heart.
  12  N C2  E CJ  S CT  W CA
      note: Only clubs are left to lose.
  13  W C9  N C8  E CK  S CQ
      note: 10 tricks: 4♥ made.

play recap:
  Declarer's plan: draw trumps, cash the side winners, then run the
  hearts.

  4♥ made. Your raise was all partner needed to hear: with the fit known,
  she could bid game.
